# Line endings are pinned to LF for every text file in this repo.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites the working
# tree to CRLF on checkout. That breaks this repo in ways that are quiet and
# slow to diagnose: a shebang line ending in CR makes a script unrunnable,
# heredoc delimiters stop matching, and `read` picks up a trailing CR in
# every variable. The scripts here are executed by bash on all three
# platforms, so LF is the only correct checkout form.
#
# The generated .cmd shims are the one place CRLF is wanted, and the
# installer writes those outside the repo.
* text=auto eol=lf
